    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T19:29:38Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure this is a bug, it's more of an observation that when the user does wildly wrong things, marginally bad stuff might occur. Similarly, if the user tests a file so large than they can't possibly store it in memory, things would break, but I don't think that it's necessary to force all sorts of OS-specific checks for available memory.",
